# oracle: w194gneb_chain_conv — the w194gneb_chain system with the verbose table and the early stop (etol 1e-7, ttol 1e-3): the
# regular stage stops at Step 54 and the climbing stage at Step 64, between rows (both stop rows printed); climber replica 3.
# GradV3dottan is NaN in native's table (the last replica's pair), so it is skipped.
# Measured with native LAMMPS: the engine's 9 table rows equal native's at the printed precision (8 significant digits) with
# max relative error 0 after rounding; unrounded, the largest difference is 4.2e-8 (GradVc), the printed digits themselves.
# The same case with thermo_modify norm yes also stops at Step 54 and 64 and matches at the printed precision. Engine 1.2 s.
# native: b332f28 (the installed lmp, SPIN and REPLICA packages)
# oracle-partitions: 4
# oracle-inputs: w194gneb_chain.data w194gneb_chain.final
# oracle-compare: rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 printed=8 skip=GradV3dottan
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style spin
atom_modify map array
read_data w194gneb_chain.data
mass 1 55.845
pair_style spin/exchange 3.0
pair_coeff * * exchange 3.0 0.02726 0.2171 1.841
neighbor 0.1 bin
neigh_modify every 10 check yes delay 20
fix 1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.1 0.0 0.0 1.0 anisotropy 0.0001 1.0 0.0 0.0
fix_modify 1 energy yes
fix 3 all neb/spin 1.0
timestep 0.0001
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g
min_style spin
min_modify alpha_damp 1.0 discrete_factor 10.0
neb/spin 1.0e-7 1.0e-3 60 60 10 final w194gneb_chain.final verbose
